s and this was the last time that Olympic competition would be contested on other than a 400-metre track. The 1924 Olympic track &amp; field events were later depicted in the Academy Award winning movie " [:em {} "Chariots of Fire"] ". The movie followed the exploits of two British sprinters, " [:a {:href "/athletes/68824"} "Harold Abrahams"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/69245"} "Eric Liddell"] ", as they prepared for and then competed at the 1924 Olympic Games. But the actual star of track &amp; field was the great Finnish distance runner " [:a {:href "/athletes/67728"} "Paavo Nurmi"] ". Nurmi won both the " [:a {:href "/results/57390"} "1,500 metres"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/57399"} "5,000 metres"] ", running those finals within an hour of each other. He also won the " [:a {:href "/results/57406"} "individual cross-country"] " and ran on winning Finnish teams in the " [:a {:href "/results/57407"} "cross-country"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/57466"} "3,000 metre team"] " races, winning five gold medals in all, still the most won by any athlete in track &amp; field at a single Olympics as of 2024."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/57285"} "100 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "6 –  7 July 1924"] "\n" [:td {} "82"] "\n" [:td {} "34"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/57315"} "200 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "8 –  9 July 1924"] "\n" [:td {} "65"] "\n" [:td {} "33"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/57345"} "400 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "10 – 11 July 1924"] "\n" [:td {} "60"] "\n" [:td {} "27"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/57375"} "800 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n